# ParcelPilot — Product Decisions & Trade-offs

## 1. Why Two AI Experiences?

| Customer AI | Support AI |
| :--- | :--- |
| Customer self-service | Internal investigation |
| Own-account data | Authorized customer data |
| Simple operational actions | Deeper investigation |
| User confirmation | Support review |

Separating the two keeps the experience focused and makes access boundaries easier to enforce.

---

## 2. Why Categories?

Categories make the chatbot easier to navigate and provide an initial retrieval hint.

| Customer | Support |
| :--- | :--- |
| Shipments | Company |
| Cancellations | Category |
| Service Credits | Subcategory |
| Tickets | Investigation |
| Product Help | |
| Account Support | |
| Other | |

Categories are **not hard boundaries**. If a question requires information from multiple areas, the AI can retrieve it.

---

## 3. Why Deterministic Confidence?

The LLM does not decide its own confidence score.

| Factor | Considered |
| :--- | :---: |
| Evidence completeness | Yes |
| Source authority | Yes |
| Freshness | Yes |
| Customer applicability | Yes |
| Conflicting sources | Yes |

| Confidence | Behaviour |
| :--- | :--- |
| **HIGH** | Answer directly |
| **MEDIUM** | Explain limitation + offer ticket |
| **LOW** | Avoid guessing + recommend escalation |

This makes confidence reproducible and easier to audit.

---

## 4. Why Human Confirmation?

AI can **prepare** an action, but the user must confirm it.

```text
AI prepares action
       │
       ▼
User confirms
       │
       ▼
Backend validates again
       │
       ▼
Action executes
```

Used for actions such as shipment cancellation and ticket creation.

---

## 5. Source Precedence

When information conflicts, ParcelPilot follows:

```text
Customer Agreement > Current Policy > Product Documentation > Historical Tickets
```

This structural hierarchy prevents outdated or incorrect historical guidance from overriding applicable customer terms.

---

## 6. What We Intentionally Left Out

| Not included | Reason |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Direct carrier integrations** | Requires external carrier APIs |
| **Full return-to-origin execution** | Requires carrier workflow |
| **Replacement shipment creation** | Outside current product scope |
| **Automatic financial credits** | Requires additional approval controls |

